

                   ADVENTURER-KINGS:  GAME 3, TURN 11

                                  FOR

                   SHAMAN UGA-BUGA MAKUMBU



         




  Quote of the Week:

  Desierius Erasmus, Dutch scholar, 1521:
  "Let a King recall that to improve his realm is better than to increase 
his territory."


ACTION REPORT    

Here's what happened to Your Majesty this turn:


  With the advent of the spring season Uga-Buga Makumb set out to quench his 
thirst for adventure.  He girded his weapon and entered the Pyramid warily.  
He encountered the Medusa.  Chanting his syllables of magic with trained 
precision, Uga-Buga Makumb let fly a Gate Demon spell and a flaming portal 
appeared, through which stepped a horrible demon!
  The Medusa speedily moved to bow range.  Weaving its silver words of magic 
into a mighty Invisibility spell, the Rakshasha waved its hands, fading into 
invisibility.  Drawing back with all its strength, the Medusa glared a 
stony gaze at the Rakshasha and missed.  The Medusa glared an angry 
stony gaze at the Rakshasha but its aim was just off the mark.
  The Rakshasha chanted its mysterious words of magic and cast a 
Mirror-Image Phantasm spell but the spell seemed ineffective against 
the Medusa.
  The Medusa closed to melee range, filled with blood-lust.  The Rakshasha 
feigned retreat, then whirled and arrogantly thrust at the Medusa and scored 
on the Medusa, doing 3 points of damage.  The Medusa lunged at the Rakshasha 
but the Rakshasha dodged the dagger.  The Rakshasha thrust at the Medusa and 
scored 3 damage points on the Medusa.  The Medusa whirled around and lunged 
at the Rakshasha and would have struck the Rakshasha if the Rakshasha hadn't 
sidestepped.
  The Rakshasha skillfully lunged at the Medusa and inflicted 4 damage 
points.  The Medusa summoned all its strength and desperately lunged at its 
vaunted nemesis but its dagger whiffed through the air.  The Rakshasha 
thrust at the Medusa with all its strength and walloped the Medusa with 4 
damage points.  The Medusa dropped to the ground, fatally pierced.  
The Rakshasha disappeared to whence the Rakshasha came.  Uga-Buga Makumb 
sacked the treasure of the Medusa.  Uga-Buga Makumb walked over to a pile of 
treasure and bagged the Large Hoard of Gold.  Uga-Buga Makumb located a 
treasure of 23 gold.
  While scouting the Pyramid, Uga-Buga Makumb saw a Crucible which seemed to 
be of a magical nature.
  Magic runes formed on the Crucible, saying "The Crucible will grant a 
minor Wish.  When you scout it, you may increase any ability by one, if your 
unmodified skill level is less than your aptitude (maximum 4).  SA-y the 
ability number (0=Tactics, 1=March etc.  , the order is shown in your 
Character List).  After the power of the Crucible is used in a gameturn, it 
may not be used again until the next gameturn.  Hello, adventurer.  You will 
now be blessed with my favor this year.  The Crucible will grant a wish to a 
character.  SA-y an ability number (not the skill name itself), and your 
skill shall be raised by one: 0-Tac, 1-Mar, 2-Nav, 3-Arc, 4-Mel, 5-Whi, 
6-Nec, 7-Ele, 8-Psy, 9-Ill, 10-Dru, 11-Thi, 12-Exp, 13-Spy, 14-Sage.  The 
Crucible cannot grant the wish if the character's skill has already reached 
his aptitude level."

