  Samantha stood ready at the head of her thousands.  No generals were 
present to lead the forces of Uga-Buga Makumb.
  Samantha was unlucky this time, because her rations were dwindling and her 
men had to fight on empty stomachs.  As the fierce battle intensified, the 
tactical wit of the acting commander and Samantha appeared to be well 
matched.
  Mugai (#3)'s soldiers swore to struggle desperately for their homeland.
  Across the whole front, the 213th Chariots faced the 6th Garrison.  The 
13th Garrison outflanked the enemy and charged in with full strength.  The 
213th Chariots fought the 6th Garrison and was almost powerless to stop 
their determined advance.
  Having found a weak point in the line of the host of Mugai, a final 
determined thrust defeated their opponent and won the day for the acting 
commander.  The 6th Garrison destroyed the 213th Chariots.
  Samantha (#95)'s armies were defeated and pushed out of Ngara.  Her forces 
completely dispersed, Samantha escaped frightened and alone to Chirfa.

  Soldiers carrying the battle-standards of the Kahn (#6)ian empire marched 
on the Forest province of the Jellyfish Sea, a land defended by the soldiers 
of Shaman Uga-Buga Makumb Stuffy doll.  Kahn was in command of the attacking 
armies.  The defending forces were commanded by the provincial garrison 
commander.  The armies were drawn up into lines of battle as shown here:

