  II Kahn marched with his loyal troops, eyes set in grim resolution.  No 
generals were present to lead the forces of Uga-Buga Makumb.
  As luck would have it, Kahn's formations were well concealed by some 
rocks, giving them a small edge.  As the fierce battle intensified, the 
tactical abilities of the acting commander and Kahn seemed evenly matched 
and neither leader could gain a tactical advantage.

  Out on the right wing, the 214th Fleet Marines faced the 287th Garrison.  
The 88th Garrison outflanked the enemy lines and charged in with full 
strength.  Here, when the commander of the 214th Fleet Marines noticed a 
weak point in the enemy line, he quickly assembled an elite force of picked 
veterans to break through it, and achieved some initial success.
  The struggle blazed with a terrible fury.  The 287th Garrison used 
wide-headed catapult missiles to cut down the enemy's catapult engines.  The 
214th Fleet Marines fought with the 287th Garrison and gradually gave 
ground.
  Out on the left outside wing, the 87th Garrison were aided in the battle 
by a band of medicine men from the League of Pagan Clerics, which aroused 
them to a fanatical zeal.  They faced the 288th Garrison.  Here, the 
soldiers of the 288th Garrison were held up by a muddy field.
  But then the tide turned.  The commander of the 87th Garrison was 
flattened by a boulder thrown from a catapult, which terribly deflated the 
spirits of the troops.  The 87th Garrison fought the 288th Garrison and was 
forced to retreat in disarray.
  Having found a vulnerable point in the line of the host of Kahn, a final 
savage slashing attack defeated their enemy and won the battle for the 
acting commander.  The 288th Garrison annihilated the 87th Garrison.
  Kahn's armies were defeated and pushed out of the Jellyfish Sea.  The 
214th Fleet Marines and the 88th Garrison were unable to retreat and were 
paroled into the general population.

  Giovanna (#7) ordered an invasion force into the adjacent Forest province 
of Maplehaven, owned by Shaman Uga-Buga Makumb Stuffy doll.  Rolando (#55)'s 
forces took Maplehaven without any major battles.  Rolando leads 
approximately 1 Legion.
  In early summer, Uga-Buga Makumb commanded the 154th Legion to remain in 
Plumwood with Clarambald.  The 154th Legion dug graves for themselves, 
unwilling to serve anyone but their master, unless given to an Undead leader 
like themselves.  Uga-Buga Makumb dropped off the 71st Legion in Plumwood 
for Clarambald.  The 71st Legion dug graves for themselves, unwilling to 
serve anyone but their master, unless given to an Undead leader like 
themselves.  Uga-Buga Makumb assigned the 233rd Chariots to Clarambald in 
Plumwood.  The 233rd Chariots dug graves for themselves, unwilling to serve 
anyone but their master, unless given to an Undead leader like themselves.
  With the coming of the late summer season, Uga-Buga Makumb rode his flying 
armies into Mare Imbrium.

  A fleet of mighty ships carried the banner of 
Shaman Uga-Buga Makumb Stuffy doll into the Sea province of Mare Imbrium, 
held by Prometeo (#5).  Mare Imbrium was conquered and occupied by 
Uga-Buga Makumb's fleet.  Mare Imbrium was found to have an income of 1 
gold.
  During fall, Uga-Buga Makumb rode his flying armies over to the Aries Sea.

  Giovanna (#7)'s forces initiated a campaign of conquest in Sageleaf, a 
Forest province owing allegiance to Shaman Uga-Buga Makumb Stuffy doll.  
Hakim (#79)'s forces experienced little resistance in Sageleaf and Hakim 
there established our rule.  Hakim leads approximately 1 Were-Beasts.
  The Aries Sea was overrun and occupied by Uga-Buga Makumb's fleet.  The 
Aries Sea was found to have a tax base of 3 gold.
  In early winter, Uga-Buga Makumb flew over to Tigerhome.  Uga-Buga Makumb 
discovered a heretofore unknown Cavern (#23) in Tigerhome, inhabited by 
the Black Dragon.  The Black Dragon has already been killed; the Cavern, 
sacked and looted.

  Thus endeth the adventures of Shaman Uga-Buga Makumb Stuffy doll for this 
year.


  Uga-Buga Makumb treated with his ally Lord Babba Sissoko Master orango 
(#0).
  Your Majesty, I have news to report of wanderers in our kingdom:  
  Robin (#51) awoke one day with a desire to see Balmwood, and so left 
Cantia to journey to that province.
  Ashley (#74) grew tired of Alderwood and left for Chandrapur.

  Cantia was plundered by the Werewolf, who stormed from out of the dark and 
pillaged or destroyed 2 gold worth of property.  Starhaven was plundered by 
the Gargoyle, who stormed from out of the dark and pillaged or destroyed 4 
gold worth of property.  The Icaria Sea was plundered by the Giant Wolverine,
who stormed from out of the dark wilderness and pillaged or destroyed 2 gold 
worth of property.  Sherwood was raided by the Centaur, who stormed from out 
of the dark wilderness and pillaged or destroyed 2 gold worth of property.
  Here is the financial report for Uga-Buga Makumb's kingdom: this turn, the 
Kingdom collected 404 gold in revenue.  70 gold was expended to finance our 
leaders.  The 56th Garrison, the 98th Mermen, the 112th Garrison, the 115th 
Garrison, the 118th Garrison, the 121st Garrison and the 127th Garrison 
trained well and improved in quality.  165 gold was expended to maintain our 
armies.  Uga-Buga Makumb was left with 484 gold in the treasury.


LETTER REPORTS

