  Giovanna stood ready at the head of her thousands.  I marched with my 
loyal troops, jaws set in terrible resolution.
  The army of Giovanna used magic to aid their cause.  Magical phantasmal 
armies fought with hers soldiers.  The Skeletal Armies led by 
Uga-Buga Makumb marched into battle with a fanatical fervor.  Giovanna 
wielded her Sword Excalibur.  She stepped forward and challenged me to 
personal combat.  I declined to enter combat.
  The forces commanded by me were dismayed by my faint-heartedness.  They 
marched on, though with lessened confidence.  My soldiers, with no camels 
for the tortuous desert, suffered from thirst.  Giovanna's luck seemed to be 
running low, as the engagement's unforeseen timing caught her soldiers 
somewhat unprepared.  Guerin's men thus gained a significant edge.  As the 
desperate battle developed, the tactical wit of Guerin and Giovanna appeared 
to be evenly matched and neither leader could gain a tactical advantage.
  Giovanna gave a rousing speech to her army, raising their morale.  She 
held aloft her Sword Excalibur and the Humans were virtually hypnotized!  
The Elves commanded by Giovanna were not impressed by her lack of leadership 
ability.
  On the right outside wing, the Crack 274th Legion sang their heroic 
ballads, inspired with a fanatical fury by their exalted King.  They were 
arrayed against the Crack 108th Bowmen.  The 274th Legion battled the 108th 
Bowmen and determinedly plowed into their opponents.
  In the interior lines, the 177th Legion faced the 292nd Legion.  Here, 
after some fighting, the commander of the 292nd Legion waved a white flag 
and offered his sword to the enemy commander.  But just as he reached out to 
accept it, he was treacherously decapitated!  At this signal, the 292nd 
Legion charged forward in a surprise attack.  The 177th Legion fought the 
292nd Legion and neither army could gain an advantage over the other.
  In the interior front, the Elite 259th Legion were aided by a Thunderbird 
who descended from the stars to aid their Divine cause, and were elevated to 
fanaticism by its divine splendor.  They faced the Elite 240th Skeletal 
Bowmen, who were encouraged to selfless fanatiscm by me, their heroic First 
Elder of Elvenkind.  The horses of the 185th Light Cavalry were spooked by 
the Beasts they were faced with.  The 124th Skeletal Dragons swooped down on 
the 185th Light Cavalry and attacked without mercy.  In this engagement, the 
259th Legion feigned retreat, hoping to lure the enemy into more suitable 
ground.  But the ruse backfired when some of the soldiers panicked, and the 
259th Legion milled about in confusion.
  But then the tide of battle reversed.  The 240th Skeletal Bowmen's luck 
turned horrible!  A meteor fell upon the 240th Skeletal Bowmen and killed 
many soldiers.  The 259th Legion fought the 240th Skeletal Bowmen and 
gradually gave ground.
  Within the interior front, the Crack 186th Legion were arrayed against the 
Green 209th Warg Riders.  The 186th Legion fought with the 209th Warg Riders 
and squashed them like rotten tomatoes.
  In the interior front, the 299th Legion sang out their fiery battle hymns, 
inspired with a fanatical fury by their exalted King.  They faced the Elite 
241st Bowmen.  In this sector, the men of the 241st Bowmen indulged in 
plundering before the contest was over, which weakened their numbers a 
little.  The 299th Legion fought the 241st Bowmen and steadily advanced 
against them.
  On the left wing, the Veteran 275th Legion faced the Crack 110th Bowmen.  
In this match, the contest was an uneventful slugfest which was decided by 
the courage of the soldiers in hand-to-hand combat.  The 275th Legion fought 
the 110th Bowmen and aggressively knifed into them.
  The forces of Giovanna broke through and were victorious.  The 274th 
Legion scattered the 108th Bowmen in all directions.  The 186th Legion slew 
the 209th Warg Riders almost to a man.  The 299th Legion demolished the 
241st Bowmen.  The 331st Bowmen chased after the enemy and were driven off 
by the 110th Bowmen after a hard-fought rearguard battle.  The 185th 
Light Cavalry overtook the enemy in their panicky retreat and annihilated 
the 292nd Legion.  The 243rd Light Cavalry gave chase and destroyed the 
110th Bowmen.
  Giovanna's host ended the campaign successfully and conquered the province 
of Rejaf.  I retired to Quantara Roo, defeated but not discouraged.
  In early summer, I cast a Bless spell.  Kajaani was magically blessed and 
prospered.  The skeletal remains of the 276th Light Cavalry were Blessed and 
permanently destroyed.
  Gladstone could not cast Phantasmal Armies on me because I was in another 
province.  So, Gladstone tried to improve his Sageness, but the task seemed 
beyond his natural ability.  He discovered nothing in his sagely 
experiments.
  Midsummer's night came and went and a hot late summer arrived.  I cast a 
Skeletal Army spell and no skeletons answered the spell's call.
  With the advent of the fall season, I cast a Bless spell.  Tigerhome was 
magically blessed and prospered.  The Bless affected no armies in Tigerhome. 
My efforts raised my prowess in White Magic.
  Congratulations!  Your kingdom has attained level 5 in White Magic.  At 
levels 5 and up, the usual 15% per level increase in the cast chance is 
discontinued, and the number of spells you can cast in White Magic is capped 
at 3 Action, 2 Combat.  The effects of the "Holy Symbol" and "Spiritwrack" 
spells are also capped at level 4 (however, skill level will still determine 
who attacks first in personal combat).  Instead, all characters of this high 
level are awarded the following Advanced Ability: 
  WHITE MAGIC- ENHANCED HOLY SYMBOL:  The Holy Symbol spell now has the same 
effect against opponents who have an Evil alignment as it does against 
Undead creatures.

  The fall cooled into a frigid early winter.  I attempted an illegal move.  
I tried to move from Quantara Roo to Kajaani, a non-adjacent province.  
Instead, I flew over to Rejaf.  While on the march, I took an interest in 
the terrain of Rejaf, exploring some unknown territory.  We have now 
explored 100% of Rejaf.

  Thy humble servant,   Guerin


