  The defenders had the 243rd Light Cavalry, the 331st Bowmen, the 21st 
Legion, the 248th Light Cavalry, the 215th Camel Corps and the 332nd Bowmen 
in reserve.  Teleko commanded a host of loyal soldiers into the battle.  
Standing tall with her warriors was Giovanna.  Rolando (#55) marched with 
his loyal troops, eyes set in grim resolution.  Drake (#44) led his armies 
into the battle.
  The army of Giovanna (#7) used magic to aid their cause.  Magical 
phantasmal armies fought with hers soldiers.  Giovanna wielded her Sword 
Excalibur.  Teleko strode forward and challenged Giovanna to honorable 
combat.  Giovanna accepted the challenge to personal combat.  Gesturing with 
her arms, she juxtaposed otherworldly forces of magic, casting a Spiritwrack 
spell, to make Teleko quake and shiver with spiritual convulsions.
  Teleko advanced to bow range.  Chanting her silver words of magic into a 
great Holy Symbol spell, Giovanna waved her arms.  A golden mist in the 
shape of a cross formed around Giovanna.  By Giovanna's special Advanced 
White Magic powers, the spell caused Teleko to moan in excruciating pain and 
inflicted 11 damage points.
  Teleko charged into melee range.  He immediately thrust at Giovanna and 
would have struck her if Giovanna hadn't ducked.  Giovanna chanted her 
strange words of magic and cast an Invisibility spell, fading into 
invisibility.  Giovanna swang at Teleko and damaged him, scoring 9 damage 
points.  Teleko dropped to the ground, fatally pierced.  And so it came to 
pass that Teleko met his tragic end.
  The forces commanded by Teleko were disheartened by his death, but still 
they moved ahead with some hope of victory.  Giovanna and the acting 
commander had both bribed some feuding native tribes to fight for them, but 
luckily for the acting commander, its allies were more adequately armed for 
their skirmishing role.  On the other hand it rapidly became apparent that 
the acting commander was tactically outmatched by Giovanna.  Giovanna 
utilized her forces brilliantly.
  Giovanna gave an inspiring speech to her army, which bolstered their 
morale.  She held aloft her Sword Excalibur and her Humans cheered wildly!  
The Elves led by Giovanna were disgusted with her strange appearance.
  On the left outside wing, the Elite 322nd Eagles were lifted to fanatical 
anger by Teleko, their honored Ace of Eagles.  They were arrayed against the 
Crack 186th Legion, who sang their thunderous battle hymns, infused with a 
spirit of righteous, fanatical fury by their exalted King.  The 322nd Eagles 
soared over the 186th Legion and attacked without mercy.  The 326th Dragons 
swooped down on the 275th Legion and attacked without mercy.  The 321st 
Eagles swooped down on the 242nd Light Cavalry and attacked them.  The 322nd 
Eagles battled with the 186th Legion and had their booties kicked up their 
throats.
  In the interior front, the Veteran 323rd Trolls faced the Elite 274th 
Legion, who were visited by a Thunderbird who flew down from the stars to 
aid their heroic Divine cause, and were inspired to fanaticism by its divine 
spectacle.  The 319th Eagles soared over the 299th Legion and attacked 
without mercy.  The 323rd Trolls fought the 274th Legion and were cut down 
like cattle.
  On the right outside flank, the Crack 320th Eagles faced the Elite 259th 
Legion, who sang their heroic ballads, infused with a fanatical fury by 
their exalted King.  The 320th Eagles soared over the 259th Legion and 
attacked them.  The 234th Dragons soared over the 177th Legion and attacked 
without mercy.  The 320th Eagles battled with the 259th Legion and were 
trampled over like overripe pumpkins.
  The battle ended victoriously for the soldiers of Giovanna as they broke 
through the lines at a critical moment.  The 186th Legion scattered the 
322nd Eagles in all directions.  The 274th Legion slew the 323rd Trolls 
almost to a man.  The 259th Legion demolished the 320th Eagles.  The 275th 
Legion annihilated the 326th Dragons.  The 299th Legion destroyed the 319th 
Eagles.  The 177th Legion scattered the 234th Dragons in all directions.  
The 242nd Light Cavalry slew the 321st Eagles almost to a man.
  The attacking Kingdom was defeated and turned back in its move to take 
Maplehaven.  The battle affected the quality of our forces:  the 323rd 
Trolls was severely mangled during the fight and has fallen in stature to 
Green condition.  Its forces completely destroyed, the acting commander 
escaped frightened and alone to the Andrea Doria Sea.  Teleko's efforts 
improved his prowess in Tactics.
  Congratulations!  Your kingdom has attained level 5 in Tactics.  At levels 5
and up, the automatic 20% per level increase in army strength is 
