  The attackers had the 297th Axemen in reserve.  I stood ready at the head 
of my ships.  No generals were present to lead the forces of the provincial 
Merman chieftain.
  Tao-Li's luck wasn't very good this time.  My superstitious men became 
unsettled when my priests were unable to properly sacrifice a bull to the 
Great Father because they had all been slain by gryphons.  On the other hand 
naval superiority was clearly assured by my powerful tactical genius.

  Across the whole front, the 147th Whales were arrayed against the 117th 
Mermen.  The 147th Whales swam undersea and attacked.  The 147th Whales were 
picked off one by one by Mermen armed with nets and barbed harpoons.
  I switched the 78th Bowmen to the fore, angling for a superior match-up.  
The 117th Mermen swam undersea and attacked.  The unshielded troops of the 
117th Mermen were sitting ducks for the lucky sharp-shooting Bowmen.  The 
78th Bowmen fought with the 117th Mermen and cut them down like weeds.
  Tao-Li's squadrons shattered the fleet opposing them with a final 
determined sally.  The 78th Bowmen demolished the 117th Mermen.
  The Cannibal Sea was conquered by the fleets of Tao-Li.
  With the advent of the early summer season, I recruited enough men in the 
Cannibal Sea to create the 98th Mermen for the army of Tao-Li.
  Midsummer's day came and went and late summer arrived.  I moved into the 
Cognac Sea (#1001) with my Fleet.  To the north is a forbidding mass of ice 
which seemingly has no end.
  The Cognac Sea was conquered and occupied by Tao-Li's fleet.  The Cognac 
Sea was found to have an income of 3 gold.
  In fall, I boldly sailed my command into Mare Actium (#901).  To the north 
lay an icy expanse which extends as far as a man can see.
  Tao-Li's naval forces took control of Mare Actium practically uncontested. 
Mare Actium was found to have a tax base of 0 gold.
  With the coming of the early winter season I sailed into the Barents Sea 
(#802) with my formidable command.

  A fleet sent by the empire of Shaman Uga-Buga Makumb Stuffy doll entered 
the Barents Sea, hoping to subjugate that province owned by 
Cosmic Herderer Mugai (#3) and made up of great Seas.  The Barents Sea was 
overrun by Tao-Li's fleet.  The Barents Sea was found to have a tax base of 1
gold.

  Thy humble servant,   Tao-Li


