From: Odysseus
To: Uga-Buga Makumb

  Honored Sovereign, 

  With the advent of the spring season I set out to quench my thirst for 
adventure.  I rode my flying armies into Sherwood.

  An army coming from the empire of Shaman Uga-Buga Makumb Stuffy doll 
invaded Sherwood, hoping to subjugate that province owned by II Kahn (#6) 
and made up of great Forests.  Odysseus's forces encountered little 
opposition in Sherwood and I there established our rule.  Sherwood was found 
to have a tax base of 10 gold.
  Windy spring blossomed into early summer.  I rode my flying armies over to 
Quantara Roo.  I marched along an unusual route through Quantara Roo and 
raised our level of exploration there to 100%.  I was informed by some 
peasants of a feature in Quantara Roo previously unknown to us, a Cavern 
(#31) inhabited by the Imp.  Legend says the Shrunken-Head Amulet is hidden 
here.  Evil magic-users say that the Imp is a weak minor devil who often 
will act as a "familiar", or magical companion, for evil characters.  I 
located a previously unheard of Crypt (#120) in Quantara Roo, held by 
the Ice Devil.  What treasure may lie there is unknown.  Legend has it that 
the Ice Devil is an extraordinarily cruel, cold and very powerful devil with 
magical powers.
  With the coming of the late summer season I flew over to Rejaf.  Rejaf had 
an illusion cast upon it.  It was actually a Desert province.

  Shaman Uga-Buga Makumb Stuffy doll ordered an invasion force into the 
Desert province of Rejaf, owned by Giovanna (#7).  Rejaf was overrun and 
occupied by Odysseus's host.  Rejaf was discovered to have an income of 1 
gold.
  With the advent of the fall season I cast a Tornado spell.  Magical 
tornadoes hit the defenders of Kajaani.  The Tornado affected no armies in 
Kajaani.
  With the advent of the early winter season, I transferred the 91st Dragons,
the 102nd Eagles, the 123rd Eagles, the 198th Trolls, the 206th Dragons, the 
249th Dragons, the 333rd Bowmen and the 334th Bowmen to Guerin in Rejaf.

  Thy humble servant,   Odysseus


From: Elmer
To: Uga-Buga Makumb

  Honored Sovereign, 

  Winter gave way to fragrant spring.  I journeyed to Cantia.  While 
adventuring, I encountered no monsters.
  In early summer, I travelled to Marzuq.  I found some time to investigate 
Marzuq while marching.  100% of it has been explored to date.  I encountered 
no wandering monsters.
  With the coming of the late summer season, I tried to explore Marzuq but 
it seemed that it had already been completely explored.  I encountered no 
monster.
  The summer mellowed into a colorful fall.  I rode into Tesawa.  During my 
travels, I was confronted by a local sheriff who apparently believed I was a 
wanted criminal.  But I wasn't listed as an outlaw, so I got off the hook.

  During early winter, I explored Tesawa and now 91% of it has been explored.
I saw no monsters.

  Thy humble servant,   Elmer


From: Presto
To: Uga-Buga Makumb

  Honored Sovereign, 

  With the advent of the spring season, I prepared to quench my thirst for 
glory.  I explored the Plesiosaurus Sea carefully, leaving no stone unturned,
and our exploration level there has risen to 100%.  I discovered a Loch 
(#109) in the Plesiosaurus Sea, occupied by the Elasmosaurus.  Legend says 
the Rod of Resurrection is hidden here.  The Elasmosaurus is a strong marine 
dinosaur, a relic of the prehistoric past, which terrorizes the lakes and 
seas of the world.  I discovered also that the Plesiosaurus Sea has been the 
site of hard-fought battles.  Brave and intrepid warriors have perished on 
its fields: the 296th Fleet (Veteran Dwarves).  My experience improved my 
aptitude in Exploring.  While adventuring, I saw no monsters.
  During early summer, I girded my weapon and entered the Tomb warily.  I 
encountered the Mummy.  Weaving my silver words of magic into a mighty 
Invisibility spell, I gestured with my hands, fading into invisibility.  I 
glided into what I thought was the treasure room of the Mummy, hands 
twitching with excitement.  I succeeded in laying my greedy hands on the 
valuable treasure.  I grabbed the Obsidian Vermin, my eyes glittering with 
greed.  I examined the Obsidian Vermin and discovered the following 
properties:
  The Obsidian Vermin enable you to cast the Plague spell of the college of 
Necromancy.  There is a certain number of charges in this item, and each 
time you cast the spell you use up a charge.  When all charges are used up, 
the item becomes useless.  The spell normally will take effect as if a 
magician with a skill level of 2 had cast the spell.

  I saw nothing special while scouting out the Tomb.  I saw no monsters.
  With the coming of the late summer season I rode into the Atlantis Sea.  
Viewing the eastern horizon, a man can see a Sea province known as the 
Seahorse Sea (#1607).  It is said that Lord Babba Sissoko Master orango is 
the ruler there.  It is known to be occupied by no races.  Southeast of here 
lies the province of Mare Serenitus (#1508), ruled by 
Lord Babba Sissoko Master orango.  It is said to be a Sea province occupied 
by no races.  To the southwest lies a Sea province called the Orca Sea 
(#1408), populated by no races.  It is ruled by 
Lord Babba Sissoko Master orango.  I saw no marauding monsters.
  During fall, I wandered freely about the Atlantis Sea, uncovering its 
secrets, and raising our exploration level in the Atlantis Sea to 100%.  I 
encountered no marauding monster.
  The fall season cooled into early winter.  I tried to explore the Atlantis 
Sea but it seemed that it had already been completely explored.  I 
encountered no wandering monster.

  Thy humble servant,   Presto


