From: Constantine
To: Uga-Buga Makumb

  Honored Sovereign, 

  In spring, I marched my forces into Balmwood (#503).  I discovered a 
heretofore unknown Glade (#51) in Balmwood, inhabited by the Centaur.  
Legend says the Large Hoard of Gold is hidden here.  Wood-Elves say that the 
Centaur is a cross-breed, with the body of a man and the trunk and legs of a 
horse.  He is a good archer and is usually friendly.
  In early summer, I moved into Katanga (#404) with my high-spirited army.
  Midsummer's night came and went and late summer arrived.  I hired the 30th 
Eagles, a mercenary army which had arrived in Katanga.
  With the advent of the fall season, I marched on Shasta (#304) with my 
command.
  During early winter, I attempted an illegal move.  I was ordered to move 
from Shasta to Orielle, further than my army could move.  So, I really tried 
hard to improve my Tactics, but I practiced in vain.

  Thy humble servant,   Constantine


From: Montgomery, Squire to Pascal
To: Uga-Buga Makumb

  Honored Sovereign, 

  In spring, Pascal marched his command into Macondo (#205).  Turning to the 
southeast, one can see a Mountain area, which is known as Transylvania 
(#206).  It is populated by Dwarves and Lord Babba Sissoko Master orango 
rules there.  Their Dwarven fighters fight in the style of Axemen.
  The wet spring blossomed into a sultry early summer.  Pascal explored 
Macondo, taking precise notes of the terrain and features, and now 61% of it 
has been explored.  Pascal was informed by some sheepherders of a perilous 
feature in Macondo, a Monastery (#114) inhabited by the Genie.  What 
treasure may lie there is unknown.  Legend-keepers revere the Genie as a 
good, powerful spirit capable of such magical feats as flying, using some of 
the five magical abilities amd they may sometimes even grant a wish.
  Pascal heard a rumor telling of a feature in Elkhome (#1501), a Glade 
where dwells the Centaur.  The Glade is reputed to contain the Holy Grail.
  With the advent of the late summer season Pascal moved into Bam Yanga 
(#105) with his army.
  During fall, Pascal roamed around in Bam Yanga, exploring the terrain 
there, and now 100% of it has been explored.
  The fall season darkened into the stillness of early winter.  Pascal 
boldly marched his forces into Maicuru (#1804).

  A conquering horde owing their allegiance to 
Shaman Uga-Buga Makumb Stuffy doll invaded the province of Maicuru, a Jungle 
area owned by Giovanna.  Maicuru was conquered by Pascal's host.  Maicuru 
was discovered to have an income of 4 gold.

  Thy humble servant,   Montgomery, Squire to Pascal


From: Gunga Din, Squire to Alaric
To: Uga-Buga Makumb

  Honored Sovereign, 

  With the coming of the spring season, Alaric set out to quench his thirst 
for adventure.  He moved into Marigold (#1803) with his army.

  Soldiers bearing the battle-standards of the Uga-Buga Makumbian empire 
marched on the Forest province of Marigold, a land defended by the soldiers 
of Giovanna.  Marigold was overrun by Alaric's host.  Marigold was 
discovered to have an income of 2 gold.
  Windy spring blossomed into early summer.  Alaric's attempted cast of the 
Plague spell was unsuccessful.
  With the advent of the late summer season, Alaric cast a Plague spell.  
Cascadia was hit by a plague.  The plague struck the 55th Garrison in 
Cascadia and destroyed them.
  The sultry days of summer surrendered to fall.  Alaric cast a Skeletal 
Army spell and no skeletons answered the spell's call.
  In early winter, Alaric moved into Pearlgate (#1703) with his army.

  An army coming from the empire of Shaman Uga-Buga Makumb Stuffy doll 
entered Pearlgate, hoping to subjugate that province ruled by Giovanna and 
made up of extensive Mountains.  Alaric commanded the attacking armies.  The 
defending forces were led by Tiffany (#87).  The armies were drawn up into 
lines of battle as shown here:

  ATTACKING ARMY, Battle of Pearlgate (1703):

 143rd/S  
  Lt Cav  
    01
          
 144th/S  
  Legion  
    01    
          
 219th/VS 
  Legion  
    01    
----------
    07    
 113th/G  
  Camels  
          
  DEFENDING ARMY

  The attackers had the 184th Skeletal Bowmen in reserve.  Alaric stood 
ready at the head of his thousands.  Standing at the ready with her warriors 
was Tiffany.
  The Skeletal Armies led by Uga-Buga Makumb marched into battle with a 
fanatical fervor.  As per Alaric's usual good fortune, Tiffany was 
recovering from injuries sustained in a minor engagement, and Alaric thus 
obtained an edge.  On the other hand his tactical maneuvers did not succeed 
as expected against Tiffany's clever counterstrokes, and his men entered 
battle with a slight tactical disadvantage.
  Giovanna (#7)'s troops swore to fight like tigers for their fatherland.
  Across the whole front, the Veteran 219th Skeletal Legion were arrayed 
against the Green 113th Camel Corps.  The 144th Skeletal Legion and the 
143rd Skeletal Light Cavalry flanked the enemy lines and charged in with 
full strength.  The nervous horses of the 143rd Skeletal Light Cavalry were 
frightened by the terrible Beasts they beheld.  The 219th Skeletal Legion 
fought with the 113th Camel Corps and crushed their heads as if they were 
eggshells.
  The battle ended victoriously for the soldiers of Alaric as they broke 
through at a crucial moment.  The 219th Skeletal Legion destroyed the 113th 
Camel Corps.
  Alaric's campaign effected the conquest of Pearlgate.  The battle affected 
the quality of our forces:  we could not have been more pleased with the 
fighting spirit of the 143rd Skeletal Light Cavalry, and we have raised its 
ranking to Veteran.  Her forces completely destroyed, Tiffany (#87) fled 
frightened and alone to Moussoro.

  Thy humble servant,   Gunga Din, Squire to Alaric


