by the werewolf is cursed to become one himself.
  With the advent of the early summer season I announced a call for 
volunteers in the El Kalaa Sea and was able to enlist the 112th Garrison to 
fight for the provincial garrison commander.
  In late summer, I explored the El Kalaa Sea thoroughly, leaving no stone 
unturned, and our exploration level there has risen to 41%.  My efforts 
improved my prowess in Exploring.
  The summer mellowed into the fall.  I explored the El Kalaa Sea and now 71%
of it has been explored.
  With the coming of the early winter season I travelled about the El Kalaa 
Sea, exploring its features.  After my efforts, 100% of it has been explored 
to date.

  Thy humble servant,   Dreux


From: Mortimer, Squire to Charious
To: Uga-Buga Makumb

  Honored Sovereign, 

  In spring, Charious moved into Dirkwood (#1201) with his high-spirited 
army.
  The wet spring blossomed into early summer.  Charious assigned the 47th 
Garrison to the provincial Dragon chieftain in Dirkwood.
  With the advent of the late summer season Charious rode into Gnarlia.
  In fall, Charious recruited enough men in Gnarlia to form the 121st 
Garrison for the army of the provincial garrison commander.
  The fall cooled into early winter.  Charious levied the 127th Garrison 
from among the population of Gnarlia, to serve under Charious.

  Thy humble servant,   Mortimer, Squire to Charious


From: Kokocala
To: Uga-Buga Makumb

  Honored Sovereign, 

  With the advent of the early winter season, I travelled to Starhaven.  
During my travels this season, I was accosted by a drunken officer who 
ridiculed the respected Kingdom of the King.  I slew him in a duel, but the 
rogue's older brother was a marshal, and he came after me!  But when I was 
taken to the judge, I showed him the official seal of the King, and was 
merely run out of town.


  Thy humble servant,   Kokocala


From: Lexington
To: Uga-Buga Makumb

  Honored Sovereign, 

  In late summer, I failed in my attempt to cast a Resurrection spell.
  The hot days of summer mellowed into the fall.  Kokocala was resurrected 
by the spell cast by me.
  With the coming of the early winter season I rode into Starhaven.  While 
adventuring, I encountered no monsters.

  Thy humble servant,   Lexington


