GENERAL INTELLIGENCE REPORT

Kingdom of Babba Sissoko (#0):
  In spring, Thorus (#45) prepared his armies to defend the Ark Royal Sea 
and the surrounding provinces.
  In spring, Tlazolteotl (#88) prepared her armies to defend Bam Yanga and 
the surrounding provinces.
  In early winter, Gabriel (#46) flew into Florence.

Kingdom of Mugai (#3):
  In early summer, Mugai (#3) travelled to Ngara.
  In early winter, a mysterious magical counterspell seemed to have impeded 
his spell.
  In early winter, Samantha (#95) rode into Ngara.

Kingdom of Prometeo (#5):
  In spring, Marlon (#68) journeyed to Tesawa.
  In spring, Girard (#15) travelled to Belladonna.
  In early summer, Girard journeyed to Marzuq.

Kingdom of Kahn (#6):
  In spring, Kahn (#6) sailed into the Jellyfish Sea (#1105) with his 
forces.
  In fall, Kahn rode into Falkenheim.
  In early winter, Kahn urged Bradipo I (#2) to improve diplomatic relations 
with his Kingdom, speaking at length of the great advantages of such an 
agreement.  After some deliberation, the offer was graciously accepted by 
Bradipo I.  Kahn (#6) treated with his ally Cosmic Herderer Mugai (#3).  
Kahn (#6) treated with his ally Hokuto (#4).  Kahn (#6) treated with his 
ally Prometeo (#5).  Kahn (#6) treated with his ally Giovanna (#7).  Kahn 
(#6) treated with his ally Circe (#8).  Kahn (#6) treated with his ally 
Agesilao (#9).
  In spring, Hawkins (#56) journeyed to Sherwood.
  In late summer, Hawkins travelled to Bronzeleaf.
  In fall, Hawkins rode into Bir Nzaran.
  In early winter, Hawkins moved into Mare Ionium.

Kingdom of Giovanna (#7):
  In spring, Giovanna (#7) moved into Rejaf (#1503) with her redoubtable 
army.
  In early summer, Giovanna marched her forces into Maplehaven (#1502).
  In late summer, the Plain terrain of Kajaani was magically made to appear 
as Mountain.  Cascadia was hit by a plague.
  In fall, Kurator (#99) journeyed to Damnonia.
  In early winter, Kurator unsheathed his weapon and entered the Tomb 
warily.  Kurator encountered the Ice Devil.  Chanting his silver words of 
magic into a mighty Holy Symbol spell, Kurator waved his arms.  A golden 
mist in the shape of a cross formed around Kurator.  The spell made 
the Ice Devil moan in excruciating pain and walloped the Ice Devil with 9 
damage points.  The Ice Devil's spell was disrupted by the event.  
The Ice Devil chanted its strange words of magic and cast a Charm spell but 
the spell seemed ineffective against Kurator.  Kurator loped along steadily 
and closed to bow range.  The Ice Devil waved its hands and gestured 
rhythmically, meaning to cast a Psychic Blast spell, but it went awry and a 
rabbit tumbled out of its sleeve instead.  Kurator took careful aim and 
fired an arrow at the Ice Devil and damaged the Ice Devil, scoring 1 damage 
points.  Drawing back with all his strength, Kurator shot an arrow at 
the Ice Devil and scored on the Ice Devil, inflicting 2 points of damage.  
Kurator shot an arrow at the Ice Devil and missed by a mile.  The Ice Devil 
thought to cast an Ice Suspension spell, but dropped a needed material 
component before the Ice Devil could make its attempt.  Kurator charged into 
the melee.  The Ice Devil daringly slashed at Kurator but its aim was 
slightly off the mark.  Kurator maneuvered to a good attacking vantage.  
Then Kurator swang at the Ice Devil and scored 1 damage points on 
the Ice Devil.  The Ice Devil swang at Kurator but Kurator evaded the claws. 
Kurator swang at the Ice Devil and inflicted 5 damage points.  Hoping to 
exploit a gap in Kurator's protection, the Ice Devil slashed at Kurator and 
would have struck Kurator if Kurator hadn't sidestepped.  Kurator faked one 
way, then switched over and swang at the Ice Devil and walloped 
the Ice Devil with 3 damage points.  The Ice Devil attacked Kurator but its 
claws whiffed harmlessly through the air.  Kurator swang at the Ice Devil 
and missed.  The Ice Devil swang at its nemesis but its aim was just off.  
Kurator then thrust at the Ice Devil but the Ice Devil dodged the blow.  
The Ice Devil swang at Kurator and would have struck Kurator if Kurator 
hadn't sidestepped just then.  Kurator whirled around and swang at 
the Ice Devil and damaged the Ice Devil, scoring 3 damage points.  
The Ice Devil maneuvered to a better defensive vantage.  Then the Ice Devil 
swang at Kurator but its claws whiffed harmlessly through the air.  Kurator 
acrobatically flipped over the Ice Devil and thrust at the Ice Devil and 
missed by a mile.  Undaunted, the Ice Devil swang at Kurator but its aim was 
slightly off.  Kurator swang at the Ice Devil but the Ice Devil dodged the 
blow.  The Ice Devil feinted one way, then switched over and treacherously 
swang at Kurator and would have hit Kurator if Kurator hadn't ducked just 
then.  Kurator circled left and attacked the Ice Devil but his sword whiffed 
harmlessly through the air.  The Ice Devil slashed at Kurator and missed 
badly.  Kurator summoned all his will and bravely thrust at his fearsome 
enemy but his aim was just off the mark.  The Ice Devil forced back Kurator 
with its aggressive tactics.  The Ice Devil then slashed at Kurator but 
Kurator dodged the claws.  Kurator feigned panic, then pivoted and 
arrogantly swang at the Ice Devil and scored on the Ice Devil, inflicting 1 
points of damage.  The Ice Devil swang at Kurator and would have struck 
Kurator if Kurator hadn't ducked just then.  Kurator maneuvered to a better 
attacking vantage.  Then Kurator thrust at the Ice Devil and scored 2 damage 
points on the Ice Devil.  The Ice Devil dropped to the ground, fatally 
pierced.  Kurator shifted his attention to the hoard of the Ice Devil.  
Kurator bagged the Large Hoard of Gold.  Kurator took 19 gold from the 
treasure of the Ice Devil.
  While scouting the Tomb, Kurator saw a Tome which seemed to be of a 
magical nature.
  Magic runes formed on the Tome, saying "The Tome will cast a Flood spell 
for a character who kneels before the Tome in prayer.  The Flood spell will 
take effect on this province.  You must pay 2 gold each time the Tome is 
used (to show that you accept these terms, a character must give two Scout 
orders when he Searches this feature.)"
  In early winter, Tiffany (#87) moved into Pearlgate (#1703) with her army. 
Standing at the ready with her warriors was Tiffany.
  Giovanna (#7)'s troops swore to fight like tigers for their fatherland.
  Across the whole front, the Veteran 219th Skeletal Legion were arrayed 
against the Green 113th Camel Corps.  The 144th Skeletal Legion and the 
143rd Skeletal Light Cavalry flanked the enemy lines and charged in with 
full strength.  The nervous horses of the 143rd Skeletal Light Cavalry were 
frightened by the terrible Beasts they beheld.  The 219th Skeletal Legion 
fought with the 113th Camel Corps and crushed their heads as if they were 
eggshells.  Her forces completely destroyed, Tiffany (#87) fled frightened 
and alone to Moussoro.
  In spring, Drake (#44) moved into Kajaani (#1603) with his army.

  In late summer, Giovanna (#7)'s forces initiated a campaign of conquest 
directed at Elkhome, a Forest province owing its allegiance to the 
provincial Ent chieftain.  Drake (#44) was in command of the invading 
armies.  The defenders were commanded by the provincial Ent chieftain.  The 
attacking Kingdom was defeated and forced out of Elkhome.
  In early summer, magical tornadoes hit the defenders of Pearlgate.  The 
Tornado affected no armies in Pearlgate.
  In late summer, Kajaani was magically flooded.
  In spring, Adhemar (#28) travelled to Quantara Roo.
  In early summer, Adhemar explored Quantara Roo.  Adhemar was informed by 
some peasants of a feature in Quantara Roo, a Sacred Rock inhabited by 
the Sphinx.
  In late summer, Adhemar journeyed to Sherwood.


END MOVES REPORT

  Congratulations!  You have reached skill level 5 in Tactics.  At levels 5 
and up, the automatic 20% per level increase in army strength is 
discontinued.  Instead, your characters of this exalted level are awarded 
the following Advanced Ability: 
  TACTICAL WARGAME MASTERY:  The chance for a unit to increase in quality 
when Practicing Tactics (or Naval) is increased by 100% (example: an Average 
unit now has a 10% chance to improve per phase).


END MOVES REPORT

  Congratulations!  You have reached level 5 in White Magic.  At levels 5 
and up, the usual 15% per level increase in the cast chance is discontinued, 
and the number of spells you can cast in White Magic is capped at 3 Action, 2
Combat.  The effects of the "Holy Symbol" and "Spiritwrack" spells are also 
capped at level 4 (however, skill level will still determine who attacks 
first in personal combat).  Instead, your characters of this exalted level 
gain the following Advanced Ability: 
  WHITE MAGIC- ENHANCED HOLY SYMBOL:  The Holy Symbol spell now has the same 
effect against opponents who have an Evil alignment as it does against 
Undead creatures.


END MOVES REPORT


